{"name":"Antarctica","hex":"#bfd2d0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Antarctica","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The southernmost continent, south of the Southern Ocean, containing the South Pole.","the Antarctic"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Antarctica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antarctica","blocks":[{"text":"Antarctica is Earth's southernmost and least-populated continent. Situated almost entirely south of the Antarctic Circle and surrounded by the Southern Ocean, it contains the geographic South Pole. Antarctica is the fifth-largest continent, being about 40% larger than Europe, and has an area of 14,200,000 km2 (5,500,000 sq mi). Most of Antarctica is covered by the Antarctic ice sheet, with an average thickness of 1.9 km (1.2 mi)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Antarctica_%28orthographic_projection%29.svg/330px-Antarctica_%28orthographic_projection%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctica","wikidata":"Q51"},{"title":"Antarctica (1983 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Antarctica  is a 1983 Japanese drama film directed by Koreyoshi Kurahara and starring Ken Takakura. Its plot centers on the 1958 ill-fated Japanese scientific expedition to the South Pole, its dramatic rescue from the severe weather conditions on the return journey, the relationship between the scientists and their loyal and hard-working Sakhalin huskies, particularly the lead dogs Taro and Jiro, and the fates of the 15 dogs left behind to fend for themselves."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/85/Nankyoku_Monogatari_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctica_(1983_film)","wikidata":"Q1316093"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Mount_Vinson_from_NW_at_Vinson_Platea